      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let $A$, $B$, and $C$ be the vertices of the diagonal and let $D$ be the origin point of the prism. This means that $B=(0+10,0+20,0+10) = (10, 20,10)$ and $D = (10,20,0)$.\n\nAB is the diagonal connecting $A$ and $B$. $A = (0,0,0)$ because the prism has zero length along each axis initially.\n\nUsing the Pythagorean Theorem, we can find the length of $AB$ by plugging $D$ and $B$ into the formula.\n\nSquare each component of $B$ to find the lengths and then sum them all up to use the Pythagorean Theorem.\n\n$\\sqrt{[10^2+20^2+10^2] = [100+400+100] = [600]}$",
