      "text": "We use the Pythagorean theorem to find the length of the diagonal. The diagonal connects opposite vertices of the rectangular prism, so our vectors cancel out. The vector for point $A$ is $\\textbf{i}$ and the vector for point $B$ is $\\textbf{i}+\\textbf{j}+\\textbf{k}$. Then we take the distance between these vectors. $\\textbf{i}+\\textbf{j}+\\textbf{k} = \\left | 1+1+1 \\right | = \\textbf{i}+\\textbf{j}+\\textbf{k}$. Using the euclidean distance formula for three-dimensions namely $\\left | \\sum {n_i}^2 \\right |^{1/2}$ we get the answer of $\\boxed{5\\sqrt{6}}$. The answer is 5\\sqrt{6}",
